.TH EFIVAR 1 "July 2026" "Gershwin Desktop Environment" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
efivar \- read and set EFI NVRAM keyboard layout variables
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B efivar
[\fIVALUE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B efivar
reads or sets the Apple
.B prev-lang:kbd
EFI NVRAM variable
(GUID \fI7c436110-ab2a-4bbb-a880-fe41995c9f82\fR).
This variable persists the keyboard layout preference across different boot
volumes, enabling operating systems to preselect a matching keyboard layout.
.PP
On Linux, the tool accesses the
.B efivarfs
filesystem at
.IR /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/ ,
automatically loading the kernel module and mounting the filesystem if needed.
On FreeBSD, it uses the
.IR efivar (8)
command.
.PP
Without arguments,
.B efivar
prints the current value.
With a
.I VALUE
argument (e.g.,
.BR de:3 ),
it sets the variable.
.SH VALUES
The value format is
.IB locale : number ,
where
.I locale
is a language/region code (e.g.,
.BR de ,
.BR en_US )
and
.I number
is a numeric keyboard layout identifier.
