.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Read the current keyboard layout setting:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set German keyboard layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar de:3
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set US English keyboard layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar en_US:0
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set French AZERTY layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar fr:1
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set Russian layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar ru:19456
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set Japanese KANA layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar ja:16384
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set Brazilian ABNT2 layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar pt_BR:128
.RE
.fi
.PP
Set Swedish layout:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar sv:7
.RE
.fi
.PP
View version information:
.PP
.nf
.RS
efivar \-\-version
.RE
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (e.g., unsupported platform, write failure).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/firmware/efi/efivars/prev-lang:kbd-7c436110-ab2a-4bbb-a880-fe41995c9f82
The EFI NVRAM variable file on Linux (efivarfs).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUDO_ASKPASS
If set, used when the tool needs to elevate privileges. The tool automatically
uses sudo when not running as root.
.SH NOTES
The xkbmap equivalents and locale column are best guesses for interoperability.
Not all EFI values have a corresponding xkbmap layout or locale mapping.
.PP
On some Linux systems, the
.B efivarfs
kernel module may need to be loaded:
.IR "sudo modprobe efivarfs" .
The tool attempts this automatically.
.PP
On FreeBSD, the
.I sysutils/efivar
port or package must be installed:
.IR "pkg install efivar" .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR setxkbmap (1),
.BR efivar (8),
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR mount (8)
.PP
